Map geometry in this directory — Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0
=================================================================

The `*.json` files in this directory contain coastline and road geometry
derived from OpenStreetMap.

    © OpenStreetMap contributors

OpenStreetMap data is made available under the Open Database License:
https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/
Any rights in individual contents of the database are licensed under the
Database Contents License: https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/dbcl/1-0/

Why this file exists, and what it does and does not cover
--------------------------------------------------------

The OSMF's licence guidance draws a line this directory sits on both sides of:

  * A **Produced Work** — a rendered image, an SVG, a screenshot of a map — may
    carry any licence. The maps `MapView` draws from this data are Produced
    Works, so nothing share-alike attaches to them or to a page that shows one.

  * A **Derivative Database** — data shipped to be read as data — stays under
    ODbL. These JSON files are exactly that: simplified geometry, in the shape a
    component reads. **The share-alike obligation attaches to these files**, and
    that is why this LICENSE is here rather than in the repository root.

The rest of this repository is MIT, and the published npm package is unaffected:
`packages/ui-kit` declares `files: ["src", "dist", "README.md"]`, so no fixture
reaches the tarball. `tests/geo-fixtures.test.ts` asserts that rather than
trusting it. The obligation attaches to this repository and to any deployed
Storybook, both of which carry this file and the attribution line the component
renders.

If you redistribute these files, or a database derived from them, keep this
notice and the attribution with them.

How the data was made
---------------------

`tools/geo/generate.ts`, which is committed and re-runnable. Overpass for the
source ways, mapshaper for the clip and a Douglas-Peucker simplification at one
pixel of the target render, coordinates rounded to four decimal places. The
reasoning is D25 in `.plan/DECISIONS.md`; the measurements are in
`.plan/research/map-tiles.md`.
